<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4228"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 16, 2005 - 3:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, I will tell you. I went to an anagram site and just started with the fisrt part of the word scramble. When the anagram came up with the word posed, I put that word in as a required word in the anagram. Then when I notinced other key words like body, lovely, club, etc, I had the anagram keep putting possible sentences together until it came up with that sentence. <BR> <BR>Then I did the same with the next group of letters. That one I solved quickly. I know they were awful sounding, but they did make sense from what has been published about BTK and his writings. <BR> <BR>I think I will try to do the previous puzzles that were sent in sometime this week. <BR> <BR>If anyone wants the link to the anagram site I used let me know. <BR> <BR>Jaden<!--/Text--></td></tr>
