<!--Post: 4259--><!--Time: 1105984855-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4259"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 10:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does RIAC stand for rat in a cage?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4259-->
<!--Post: 4260--><!--Time: 1105987201-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4260"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 10:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Poking, <BR>That was impressive. Seems like it could be anyone writing that though, anyone who knows enough. If BTE really is taking time to make these puzzles, you&#39;d think he&#39;d include info that proves who he is. Anyway, the only word that doesn&#39;t seem to make sense is &#34;loot&#34;. Do you think this could be another &#34;tool&#34;, one word for tools that make him look like a repairman, and then one for his own tools? Sounds stupid to repeat oneself, but let&#39;s consider the source.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4260-->
<!--Post: 4266--><!--Time: 1105991428-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4266"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->So Far<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 11:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I get: <BR> <BR>I need to pose one new body so victim is heel joined to toe <BR> <BR>unclean hose by a yellow wall <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4266-->
<!--Post: 4268--><!--Time: 1105992697-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4268"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 12:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The posting times in the last two messages were exactly 2:40 a.m. <BR> <BR>Whoever this individual is, they timed it exactly to the minute. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4268-->
<!--Post: 4269--><!--Time: 1105994390-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4269"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 12:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;d say &#34;loot&#34; is the last thing he did - as in take his &#34;treasures&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4269-->
<!--Post: 4273--><!--Time: 1106005557-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4273"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 3:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found this site where RIAC stands for -Rule induction algorithm based on approximate classification. This is way beyond my comprehension. Could someone with an advanced degree look at this site and see if there is a possible connection. <BR> <BR><a href="http://citeseer.ist.psu.edu/hamilton96riac.html" target=_top>http://citeseer.ist.psu.edu/hamilton96riac.html</a> <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4273-->
<!--Post: 4275--><!--Time: 1106009146-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4275"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 4:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looks like it&#39;s an author-proposed acronym for their own method related to artificial intelligence and knowledge theory &#40;IT stuff&#41;.  It might be useful by some sort of extension in cryptanalysis &#40;code-breaking&#41;, but I found no evidence of any such &#40;reported&#41; use by simple Google.  If the poster were BTK, and it was being used as such as some sort of clue in how to decipher the message, it would mean that BTK had developed some novel crypto methodology - which I think is not likely. <BR> <BR>But I think you&#39;re on the right track chasing down RIAC as a message key of some sort.  If not that, then it has some other important meaning, possibly verifying either the message or hinting at its BTK-ness.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
