<!--Post: 5589--><!--Time: 1107210385-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5589"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->kerri<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 2:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->good point Q- but also keep in mind that &#34;we&#34; meaning ordinary citizens, do not have a God given right to judge mens crimes here on Earth...that was explained to me by my pastor after 9/11 when a lot of people wanted to take the law into theri own hands.  This is why we&#40;meaning the U.S.&#41; have the police, FBI, court system etc.  that is their job to judge crimes and Gods alone to judge souls.  I absolutely agree that Jesus cares about and, yes even loves BTK just as he loves all of His creation.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
