<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5738"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 7:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s a thought. <BR> <BR>When BTK &#40;beeteekay&#41; says look &#34;in between&#34;, maybe it does not mean geographically.  Everyone is scouting Seneca like there was no tomorrow.   <BR> <BR>What if it means date-wise?  The date of the 8th drop was on the 17th?  The 7th drop on the 8th? <BR> <BR>I agree with the date of the 8th drop- but not the date of the 7th drop.  It would have been found - maybe.  He was too interested in listing that date on his postcard.  It meant something besides the obvious. <BR> <BR>Turn to the 12th or the 13th.  The dates &#34;in between&#34; that is. <BR> <BR>Did something significant happen on one of those two dates, linking to BTK?  Not that I know of - but if there WERE something - where would we find it? <BR> <BR>KAKE, of course. <BR> <BR>KAKE has some little doo-dads on those dates - a chase, but too young of a guy,  stuff like that.  Then they have some cancellations.  Mostly church cancellations. <BR> <BR>Looking back on this board - one poster is discussing big, old copy machines, and making drops in churches, and the direction NW. <BR> <BR>What if, just what if, the answer to the mystery, is in one of the churches in that NW direction, in their big old ancient copy machine.  One of the churches from the cancellation list on the dates &#34;in between&#34;? <BR> <BR>Wouldn&#39;t that be a hoot? <BR> <BR>Too late tonight to do any sluething.  I suppose it will have to wait for the morrow.  &#60;yawn&#62; <BR> <BR>Hey - it&#39;s as good as the skillet idea someone is running on AMW.  Besides, their &#39;skillet&#39; photo looks like a Q-tip, to me.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
