<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5807"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 3:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting ArmC.  Really interesting. <BR>Thanks for sharing.  I am saving the link you provided. <BR> <BR>There seems to be some concern with the a sign circled...found a couple of things that might arouse some interest...I do wonder if BTK is not Russian, Japanese or...German.... <BR>-------------------------------------------------- -------------------------------------------------- ---- <BR> <BR><a href="http://proofhouse.com/cm/codes_markings.htm" target=_top>http://proofhouse.com/cm/codes_markings.htm</a> <BR>Codes and Markings <BR> <BR>btk WW-II German ordnance code assigned to Aluminium-Werke Honsel, Werdohl, Germany <BR>================================ <BR> <BR>The search terms I used to find the above linguistics link were &#34;What does Russian abbreviation BTK refer to?&#34;...and look what I got...the a...with a circle... <BR> <BR>  <BR>LINGUIST List 11.1740: The &#34;@&#34; Sign  - ... having mixed it up with the English abbreviation for the ... three variants of the thing in modern Russian: 1&#41; obez ... As my Anjal does not function I cannot write it ... <a href="http://www.ling.ed.ac.uk/linguist/issues/11/11-1740.html" target=_top>http://www.ling.ed.ac.uk/linguist/issues/11/11-174 0.html</a> <BR>=================================== <BR>Just for fun.... <BR>  <BR> SERIAL KILLERS LIST 2  - ... P. Franklin &#40;15&#41; A former Klansman and neo-Nazi, Franklin was ... the Freight Train Riders of America, a boxcar gang that preys upon fellow rail-riding hobos ... <a href="http://crezimunky.lunaticsworld.com/serial%20killers%20list%202.htm" target=_top>http://crezimunky.lunaticsworld.com/serial%20kille rs%20list%202.htm</a> <BR>---- <BR> <BR>I wonder what &#39;the clues in between&#39; mean..if the poster who says  &#34;...search for the clues in between. There you would find the answer to my mystery,&#34; is actually BTK.  <BR>I am sure everyone would have his or her own idea of what BTK refers to as &#39;the clues in between&#39;.  But...the surnames he left are these: <BR> <BR>Kent T. Billingham <BR> <BR>T. Bob Kreisch <BR> <BR>Christ On the Cross <BR> <BR>B.T.K <BR> <BR>- <BR> <BR>^ <BR> <BR>440 <BR> <BR>RIAC <BR> <BR>BTK <BR> <BR>BeeTeeKay <BR> <BR>=================== <BR> <BR>Not much anyone can really make of those...but I look at the #440 and almost assume the RIAC is misspelled.  So I do a search using only three of the surnames that I consider significant.  Kreisch, 440, and RIAC.  I actually use RIAC instead of RICA in my search...and the search comes back to me with the question --&#34;Did you mean Kreisch 440 RICA&#34;? <BR> <BR>So I go to that link...and... <BR>I get these two links...looks like Dutch or something...and then I go to entry #440...this looks like a message board discussing some kind of terrorist group... <BR>Gästebuch  - ... 455&#41; Shano Crew aus Costa Rica schrieb am 10.11 ... 440&#41; RED LION SOUND aus Switzerland schrieb am 30.09 ... Angeblich war Sly Dunbar &#40;KREISCH!!!&#41; mit on stage, dass ... <a href="http://www.ruff-song.de/guestbook.php" target=_top>http://www.ruff-song.de/guestbook.php</a> <BR>  <BR>die wunderbare welt des farin u.  - ... 434] [435] [436] [437] [438] [439] [440] [441] [442 ... 32 | FLO, langsam gefällt mir die Frisur &#42;kreisch&#42; &#40;noch 2 ... 21:56 | Nunatak &#40;Ouro Preto, Vila Rica, man darf ... <a href="http://www.farin-urlaub.de/guestbook.php3?seite=423&amp;alle=1" target=_top>http://www.farin-urlaub.de/guestbook.php3?seite=42 3&amp;alle=1</a> <BR>  <BR>The way these #&#39;s are aligned to represent POSTS &#40;GOD...why am I suddenly reminded of the &#34;POST Toasties cerial box...?? LOL...&#41;... <BR>POST #440 is in another language...but look at some of the recognizable words...&#40;refer to the second link above for display of numbers that refer to many posts....interesting..&#41;Here is the first one of #440.. <BR>--- <BR> <BR>------------------------------- <BR>endlich gehts wieder nach haaauuuse! &#34;oh berlin berlin berlin, du bist aller städte queen! berlin istdufte, berlin ist stark!&#34;  <BR>ums mal mit den worten nina hagens zu sagen.  <BR> <BR>@ members: heute abend wird erst gerockt und dann gefeiert! ich will nicht vor sonntag mittag auf dem heimweg sein... &#42;d&uuml;deld&uuml;&#42;  <BR> <BR>many kisses an den blonden <BR>16.08.2003, 10:03 | Flammen-Lady &#40;fourth member of the &#40;w&#41;holy church of klugscheißering and extrem leute besuching&#41; &#40;noch&#40;!!!&#41; downtown &#42;haha&#42; krupunder... DAS ist provinz, baby!, Deutschland&#41;  <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR>The second poster on #440 shows a link to a website...called..Casket Crew Germany... <BR>und zwar die Welt von Lady Bondage!  <BR>  <BR> <BR>Mehr oder weniger schnell entsteht hier meine neue Page... also, immer mal wieder reinschauen - und Geduld haben! &#40;Aber das kennt Ihr ja, oder? &#42;g&#42;&#41; Ich arbeite dran...  <BR> <BR> <a href="http://www.casket-crew.germany.de.vu" target=_top>http://www.casket-crew.germany.de.vu</a> <BR> <BR>=========== <BR>Go to the link and see for yourself...just interesting...thanks... <BR> <BR>  <BR>=============== <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
