<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5877"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->wondering now<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 6:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Crying Game posted under messages to btk that he thought btk lived south of zoo blvd and west of meridian.  I have been looking at the map of the murder scenes and where the victim&#39;s cars were found located on another website, and it does seem that the direction that btk drove in after he left the victim&#39;s homes to where he parked his car do seem to be heading in a certain direction.  It made me think.  If someone had just killed someone and wanted to get home as quickly as possible to hide stolen mementos, change clothes, and clean up any evidence that may have been carried from the crime scene, wouldn&#39;t he try to take make as much as a beeline from where he parked the victim&#39;s cars to his home as possible?  If you follow that logic and follow the directions btk took from the crime scenes to where he parked the victims cars, including Vicki Wegerle&#39;s, it seems that south of zoo blvd and west of meridian is very plausible.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
