<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5947"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jack5150<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jack5150<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 12:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While I don&#39;t believe any of those posting are actually BTK, I may have figured out why the poster using the name &#34;440&#34; chose that name. <BR> <BR>Usually written as 4-4-0, this term refers to a railway locomotive featuring four leading wheels, four drive wheels, and no trailing wheels.  This particular configuration was known as American Standard. <BR> <BR>My guess is that this is supposed to tie in to BTK&#39;s claim to be a railroad fan.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
