<!--Post: 6239--><!--Time: 1107625894-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6239"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 9:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cougar, I agree. I personally believe that he has posted &#40;i don&#39;t think he could resist&#41;, but that he feels no need to legitimize himself to this board. This site already talks about him, so in a sense he&#39;s a celebrity without making much effort. <BR>  He&#39;s apparently saving his efforts and evidence for the police, whom I think he enjoys messing with the most. He had to know that the police wouldn&#39;t tell the public what was in the box, yet he made no effort to communicate the contents to the public. <BR>   I don&#39;t think he much cares to scare the public generally, or he&#39;d make overt communications to the public indicating that he plans to kill again. He won&#39;t do that, because ultimately it would remind citizens that now he is just a mid-life crisis-suffering plagiarist with a sexual asphyxiation hang-up.  <BR>  <BR>On the other hand, the most recent posts on the &#34;messages from&#34; thread are very brief, and he&#39;s shown himself lately to be pretty wordy in his correspondence to the police and media. It&#39;s probably not him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6239-->
<!--Post: 6259--><!--Time: 1107641641-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6259"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 2:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoever it is posting as BTK is a f&#39;ing idiot...if you are BTK, tell us what was on the 2/2 post card to KAKE and what your little symbol is...if not, grow up...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6259-->
<!--Post: 6241--><!--Time: 1107628434-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6241"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 10:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Anyone, I am having problems bringing up the puzzles.  So, I have a limited knowledge of the topic.  However, I have been working with puzzles left on the &#34;Messages From BTK&#34; board.  I figured this would be the best place to post my information, and I noticed something as soon as I read your guys&#39; posts.  The number 440 standouts to me because someone posted a message from 440 on the &#34;from BTK&#34; board &amp; 440 coincides with one of the English classes offered at Wichita State &#40;p.j.&#41;!  Wichitaboy says 440 is also an area code in Ohio.  Well, I was able to find a ZIP code for Jewel, Ohio from one of the messages on the &#34;from BTK&#34; board.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6241-->
<!--Post: 6355--><!--Time: 1107724344-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->ZENITH<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 1:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is really nothing in any of the posts &#34;from BTK&#34; to indicate it really is BTK. I think it is far too risky for BTK to post from home even if he&#39;s savvy enough to mask his IP. And remember, the biggest issue BTK faces in today&#39;s world, that wasn&#39;t an issue 20 years ago, is that there are cameras literally everywhere. 20 years ago you could park your car in a store parking lot, walk to a victim&#39;s home, kill them, then take their car back to where you left your car, and get away with it. Today you would likely have been caught on one or more cameras. <BR> <BR>Same thing about using cyber-cafes for posting. If you want to get caught on camera, use a cyber-cafe. Using PCs from within businesses, or those of acquaintances, also not too likely since it would be harder to mask your IP on multiple systems, and if any of those systems were tracked, it would get you very close to the person who accessed that/those PCs - too risky. <BR> <BR>You&#39;re on camera in Wal-Mart and in the Wal-Mart parking lot, you&#39;re on camera in most businesses of any size. They&#39;re everywhere. That&#39;s why you&#39;re seeing drops in parks and on lonely roads, that&#39;s why the notes are being mailed, and that&#39;s also why it&#39;s highly unlikely he&#39;s posting on this board. I hope he is, but I doubt he is. Because in my opinion he isn&#39;t trying to get caught. He&#39;s just enjoying having fun with KAKE and WPD, and now with Charlie and Tom.  <BR> <BR>The person posting all these rapid &#39;from BTK&#39; posts recently is just toying with everyone, and like it or not, it&#39;s not illegal to pretend to be BTK on a discussion board. Just another weirdo getting their jollies from acting up. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6355-->
<!--Post: 6356--><!--Time: 1107725195-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 1:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wish someone could prove you right?  I do.  Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6356-->
<!--Post: 6360--><!--Time: 1107728233-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6360"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 2:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think zenith is right, he&#39;s not posting on the &#34;from btk board&#34;. He said he left Vickis and walked down arrowhead and iroquois, but her car was left in the opposite direction. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
