<!--Post: 6366--><!--Time: 1107729906-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6366"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 2:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty <BR> <BR>But in the &#34;from BTK&#34; thred it was posted that: <BR>I still remember my favorite, Vicki Wegerle. I did not plan this one per se as I had the others…a &#34;lapse of control&#34; I always called that one, felt the best as well. I strangled her and left…BUT I CAME BACK! I took one more picture and then walked away…yes down Arrowhead St. <BR> <BR>As I understand this post, he LEFT by car BUT returned to the house &#40;by foot?&#41; and LEFT by foot walking down Arrowhead, turning left on Iroquois.  <BR> <BR>Here is tha quote &#34;from BTK&#34; thred: <BR> <BR>She looked disgustingly pretty so I took a few pictures...ahhh fall is the season. It had been a spur of the moment transaction. I whooped like an indian walking down Arrowhead, turning left on Iroquois. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
