<!--Post: 6387--><!--Time: 1107747777-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6387"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 7:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, now I just think that it&#39;s funny that someone &#40;I seriously doubt that it is BTL&#41; is writing that we&#39;re all way off. Unless BTK is Mr.T, then SOMEBODY on here was right at some point. I think every possible avenue has been discussed here, and even more likely by WPD. There are a finite number of actual possibilities about what race, gender, nationality, and age BTL is, so--if the idiot posting as BTK might consider the math of probabilities--someone here has been right on the money. The only think more loserly than BTK himself is the loser pretending to be him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
